  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></math>. It is given that the fundamental periods of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are <math><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> respectively, then the minimum value of <math><msub><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is"
  },
